{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"357fb37abe8316d8541b972a0babd4e1bba26beb24f5060143bf03989d8b781d","digest":{"component_or_area":"capabilities.py — verdict tier assignment","key_entities":["capabilities.py:307-311","capabilities.py:384","capabilities.py:434","capabilities.py:439","config.py:214-241","KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES","_GATEWAY_PROVIDER_NAMES","gateway/anthropic","gateway/bedrock","gateway/google-cloud","gateway/groq","gateway/openai","tier","base_url","endpoint_host","ProviderSession.provider_factory","pydantic_ai.providers.infer_provider","test_verdict_provenance.py:264","test_capabilities_module_still_has_no_provider_name_prefix_matching"],"problem_keywords":["gateway provider","tier misrepresentation","provenance attestation","signed verdict","opaque intermediary"],"propositions":["A gateway/* provider without base_url is stamped tier=first_class despite carrying traffic through an intermediary that can rewrite requests, misrepresenting provenance in signed verdicts.","The tier assignment logic derives tier only from base_url presence, ignoring that gateway/anthropic, gateway/bedrock, gateway/google-cloud, gateway/groq, and gateway/openai are live providers admitted in KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES and delegated to pydantic_ai.providers.infer_provider.","Gateway runs should be stamped tier=best_effort to signal that provenance attestation is weakened by an opaque intermediary, consistent with the existing docstring rationale for base_url-less runs.","The endpoint_host field should remain None for gateway providers unless base_url was explicitly configured, to avoid synthesising a value that nobody set."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-